For a **generic C++ application** that may eventually have Console, GUI, or REST interfaces, use this architecture:


                         APPLICATION
                              │
              ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐
              │               │               │
              ▼               ▼               ▼
        ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐
        │ Console  │    │   GUI    │    │ REST API │
        │    UI    │    │   UI     │    │   API    │
        └────┬─────┘    └────┬─────┘    └────┬─────┘
             │               │               │
             └───────────────┼───────────────┘
                             ▼
                   ┌──────────────────┐
                   │   Application    │
                   │    / Service     │
                   │      Layer       │
                   └────────┬─────────┘
                            ▼
                   ┌──────────────────┐
                   │   Domain / Core  │
                   │  Business Logic  │
                   └────────┬─────────┘
                            ▼
                   ┌──────────────────┐
                   │ Repository /     │
                   │ Data Access      │
                   └────────┬─────────┘
                            ▼
              ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
              ▼             ▼             ▼
          ┌────────┐   ┌──────────┐   ┌─────────┐
          │ SQLite │   │PostgreSQL│   │  Redis  │
          └────────┘   └──────────┘   └─────────┘


### Generic layers

Presentation
     ↓
Application / Service
     ↓
Domain / Business Logic
     ↓
Repository / Data Access
     ↓
Infrastructure / Database

### Dependency direction

Console ──┐
GUI ──────┼──→ Application → Domain
REST ─────┘                    ↓
                         Repository Interface
                                ↓
                    Infrastructure / Database

The key principle is:

> **UI should depend on your application/core, not the other way around.**

So your core does **not** contain:

cout
cin
Qt
QML
HTTP
REST
JSON

Those belong to the outer layers.

This lets you start with:

Console → Core

and later add:

GUI → Core
REST API → Core

without rewriting the business logic.
